Sval: the content classifier holds a channel until its engines are built

content-classifier-skips-url-classifier.patch skips the URL classifier
whenever the content classifier service exists, which it does before any
engine is built, so a request at startup could pass with no rule to match
it. The service holds each channel's lookup until the engines from what is on
this device are built: the passes begun before then, the Remote Settings
client's initial import among them, read Sval's lists and Remote Settings'
local copy and never the network, and a pass that fails still ends the wait.
The wait sits inside AntiTrackingChannelClassifierUtils::CheckChannelHelper;
no chrome API can hold a channel there.

